    "v2": "Direction fix: '\u092a\u094d\u0930\u093e\u092a\u094d\u0924 \u0939\u0941\u090f', 'mile hain', 'credit ho jayega', 'received from' no longer count as money-in by themselves; they need the user named as recipient or a non-user sender in the same sentence. Found via a benign Hindi bill-receipt template (merchant_bill_hi_07) hitting the amount-mismatch floor; because it was found by looking at evaluation failures, the separate validation set is the cleaner check that it generalises. Measured effect on synthetic data: benign hard-floor hits 6 -> 0 (all merchant_bill_hi_07); scam hard-floor hits unchanged (231); digital_arrest_hien_01 loses reward_claim on 10 rows ('drugs mile hain' = 'drugs were found', which v1 misread as money-in)."
  },
